WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.800
I have been sent by the Great One!

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.230
I declare death unto you!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:15.780
The Great One has mobilized
an army to destroy you!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.660
Nonetheless,
time has been granted unto you

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.210
to allow you to mount a desperate,
albeit futile resistance!

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.500
Eight days from this day--

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.340
at that time, you shall be
the second offering of death

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.920
from among the
Lizardmen tribes of this lake!

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:34.880
The second?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.510
Offer your desperate resistance,

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:43.390
so that the Great One
may sneeringly take delight!

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.310
By no means forget! Eight days!

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.240
You remember the clouds
that covered the heavens, right?

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.160
That was likely fourth tier magic,

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.540
"Green Claw Tribe"
"Head Priestess"

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.540
"Control Cloud."

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.540
"Green Claw Tribe"
"Chief Shasuryu Shasha"

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.100
Fourth tier?

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.460
Only a powerful magic caster
could use something of that scope.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.340
Even I can only use as high as second tier.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.800
We should evacuate as soon as possible.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.180
"Green Claw Tribe"
"Head Warrior"

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.180
Are you saying we should run away
before we even start fighting?!

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.220
"Green Claw Tribe"
"Head Hunter"

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.270
That thing said we had eight days.
We still have time,

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.690
so I believe we should wait
and see what the enemy does.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.640
Hmm...

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:36.150
If the choice is between running
and fighting, I choose the latter.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.570
Zaryusu, a traveler such as
yourself may not speak.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.530
You should be grateful
we're even allowing you in here--

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.710
We are allowing anyone with
any learning to participate right now.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.500
It would be wrong not to listen
to the opinions of travelers, as well.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.340
But Chief, you can't treat him special
simply because he's your brother.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.930
Not listening to the words of
the knowledgeable is the act of a fool.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:04.370
No warrior would turn away the opinion
of he who possesses Frost Pain.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.810
Hmm... So, what makes you say that?

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.310
It is the only way.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.690
Can we win?

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:16.860
Of course we can!

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.950
No. As things now stand,
our chances of winning are slim.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.740
What are you talking about?

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.700
Our foe must be aware of our forces,

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.120
which is why he has
taken the tone that he has.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.000
If so, we need to throw his reckoning off.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.340
You all remember
the war we fought earlier, right?

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.880
--Of course.
--There is no way we could forget it.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.890
There were once seven tribes
living in this marsh.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.100
There was our tribe, the Green Claw.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.850
The skilled hunters of the Small Fang.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.890
The tribe with the best
defensive capabilities, the Razor Tail.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.520
The war-loving Dragon Tusk.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.480
The moderate Yellow Speckle.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.650
The Sharp Edge, who were
proficient with sword skills.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.910
With many members possessing
priestly abilities, the Red Eye.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.790
It was several years ago that we had
an extended shortage of food,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.160
and all of our tribes
began competing with each other.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.830
Until finally, it turned into
an all-out war among the three tribes

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.630
consisting of ourselves,
the Small Fang, and the Razor Tail

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.330
against the two tribes of
the Yellow Speckle and the Sharp Edge.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.090
As a result, the three of us secured victory,

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.930
and the two losing tribes
were absorbed into the Dragon Tusk,

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.180
who remained out of the fighting.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.680
What about it?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.850
That thing said that
this village would be second.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.440
Doesn't that mean that he intends
to destroy us and the other tribes in order?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.300
You want us to join forces
with the other tribes before he attacks,

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.070
and engage him all together?

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.030
Our one-time allies,
the Small Fang and the Razor Tail,

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.780
will probably form an alliance with us again.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.080
Let there be no mistake.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.830
What I'm suggesting entails 
<i>all</i> of the tribes.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.460
Chief, I propose that we form an alliance

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.590
with the Dragon Tusk
and the Red Eye, as well!

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.260
--Impossible!
--The Dragon Tusk contains the survivors

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.340
of the two losing tribes from the last war.
There can be no alliance with us.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.150
We have no interaction 
with the Red Eye, either.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.720
Won't this be difficult?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.730
A five-tribe union...

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.610
All right. Who will be
the envoy to those two tribes?

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.110
I will go.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.110
You, a traveler?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.410
That's right. If they are unwilling
to listen to me because I'm a traveler,

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.120
then they aren't worth teaming up with.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.370
Hmm...

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.870
You'll take the chief's seal.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.640
My gratitude.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:47.980
Brother...

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.710
Rororo!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.240
I've always thought that you should have
been the one to become chief.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.540
The reason I was able
to learn how to farm fish

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.620
is because you allowed me
to be a traveler, Brother.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.750
Why would you say such a thing now?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.460
You could have done that
even if you'd stayed in the village.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:26.630
It's bright men like you who should
shoulder the weight of the village.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.630
Brother...

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.680
So, is this really all you're after?

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.310
What do you mean?
What are you trying to say?

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.810
The fact that the skirmishing
between our tribes had diminished,

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.070
as well as that our numbers had increased,

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.070
proved to be
among the causes of the past war.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.620
Brother, I think that's all you'd better say.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.580
I knew it.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.830
There's no other way if we're going to
avoid repeating that last war.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.590
In that case, what will you do
if the other tribe refuses an alliance?

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:05.210
If that happens, we'll 
eliminate them... first.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.840
You're saying you would
kill our fellow kinsmen?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.350
--Brother...
--I <i>do</i> understand you.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.180
It's the survival of the tribe.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:16.990
What happens if the man
at its head doesn't consider that?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.520
Rororo!

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.520
Let's head out.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.660
So tell me, Brother, what will the count be?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:34.700
Ten from the warrior class,
12 hunters, 3 priests,

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:39.670
70 males, 100 females,
and some of the children, I would say.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.250
Understood.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.170
If it comes to it, I'll use
those numbers as a bargaining tool.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.550
Hmm, he's sure gotten big, huh?

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.930
He was a lot smaller when I found him.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:01.770
That's hard to believe.
When you brought him back to the village,

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.190
he was already pretty big.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.280
Be sure to come back safely.
Don't do anything crazy.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:17.700
Of course not. I will see this through
to perfection and come home.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.600
Just sit tight, Brother!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.170
Hmm...

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.850
It has been far too long, Assistant Butler.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:41.020
Oh, it <i>has</i> been a long time, Lord Demiurge.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.980
Is Lord Ains around?

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.150
No, he said he would be
at the human village for several days.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.900
Lady Albedo is inside, however.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:51.990
I see. By the way, Eclair,

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.280
it's unusual for
an assistant butler such as yourself

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.410
to come all this way here.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.410
Lord Sebas is not around right now,

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.950
so I must work twice as hard
to make up the difference.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:04.170
As such, I just finished making some
specific arrangements with Lady Albedo.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.750
I guess you're right. Now that he is gone,

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:10.260
Nazarick's ninth floor
is in your capable hands.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.220
Absolutely.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:18.310
I must work hard for the time when
I rule the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.810
Right you are, keep at it.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:26.310
Your creator, Lady Ankoro Mocchi Mochi,
did design you that way.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.400
So, what is the first thing
you're going to do toward that end?

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.700
Hmph, cleaning.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.830
There is no one in Nazarick
who can clean more carefully than I can!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:48.540
After I've cleaned the restroom,
you can lick the bowl!

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.550
Outstanding!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.610
"Red Eye Tribe Village"

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.450
I am Zaryusu Shasha
of the Green Claw tribe!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.450
I would like to speak
to the Red Eye tribal chief!

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:26.170
Zaryusu Shasha of the Green Claw tribe,

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.340
the one who holds
the tribe together will see you.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.410
Hmm? Not the chief?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.350
In here.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:47.140
The one who holds the tribe together
wishes to speak with you one-on-one.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.100
Ho...

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.980
I am Zaryusu Shasha
of the Green Claw tribe!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.060
I will now enter the room.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:57.990
Please.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.870
Thank you for coming.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.760
Even the bearer of Frost Pain,
one of the Four Great Treasures,

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.470
appears to find my body bizarre-looking.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.350
Er, um, is something the matter?

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.650
Oh, I mean... That was... Please excuse me.

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:40.740
N-Not at all. I am the acting chief
of the Red Eye tribe,

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.620
Crusch Lulu.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.710
Now, may I ask the reason
for your visit here today?

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.960
Marry me.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.720
M-Marry you?

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.510
Th-That is was not
my purpose in coming here!

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:08.310
I am well aware that ordinarily
I should settle that matter first

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.980
before saying such a thing,

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.980
but I cannot be untrue to my own feelings!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:15.860
Uh-huh...

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:20.860
Ah! Oh, I'm sorry! Feel free to
give me your answer at a later date!

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:29.790
Should I not be surprised that
you are unafraid of my white body?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:36.340
From time to time among the Red Eye,
an albino such as myself is born.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.130
They grow to exhibit
an aptitude for some talent--

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:42.260
in my case, that would be priestly powers.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:46.640
For that reason, they end up
having authority second only to the chief.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.890
As white as the snow
blanketing yonder mountains.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.930
Huh...?!

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.690
It's a pretty color.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.940
Wh-What are you saying?

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.370
Wh-Why would you do that
without any warning?!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:17.630
It's love at first sight.
Plus, we might be killed in this battle,

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.580
and I wouldn't want to regret
what might have been.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:24.610
The bearer of that sword,
Frost Pain, is prepared to die?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.390
Did you see the monster
that delivered the message?

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:29.260
Yes.

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:32.770
That thing produced screams
that rattled the mind,

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:36.980
and could neutralize just about
any attack by non-enchanted weapons.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:41.110
When I encountered it before,
I had no choice but to flee.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:46.620
We druids can temporarily
imbue swords with magic.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.620
Can you ward against mental attacks?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.790
Most priests can bolster one's resistance.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.920
However, when it comes to
protecting the mind from confusion,

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.630
I'm the only one in our tribe who can do so.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.840
What number did it say
the Red Eye tribe was?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.930
It said we were the fourth.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:11.110
I see. So, what are you planning to do?

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.610
I'm going to be straight with you.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.690
If the Red Eye tribe evacuates,

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:23.210
do you think you can live the same way
you do now in some strange location?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.240
It <i>would</i> be quite difficult.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:30.910
So then, if all five tribes in the area
were to similarly evacuate,

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.750
what do you think would happen?
If we could not find enough food,

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.040
and the fish that make up
our principal diet grew scarce,

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.500
would all five tribes end up
killing each other this time?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:45.420
You don't mean fighting a battle
we may not be able to win would be...

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:50.510
Yes. I'm taking into account depopulation,
including the other tribes.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:56.100
Crusch Lulu, the Green Claw
requests an alliance with the Red Eye.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.730
If you refuse,

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:04.150
it will become necessary for us
to challenge your tribe to battle first.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.450
To prevent any one tribe
from running away without fighting

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.870
and establishing a numerical superiority
in a new land, right?

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:14.160
My thinking is that if we form an alliance,
then even if we are defeated,

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.750
the chances of intertribal warfare
in a new land are low.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.040
Our recognition of each other
will be redefined,

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.260
not as separate tribes, but as allies
who fought alongside each other.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.010
That follows.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:28.920
Incidentally...

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:33.180
...during the previous battle,
in which the Red Eye did not fight,

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.270
how did you manage to survive?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.270
Do I really have to say?

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:42.020
I'd like you to tell me. 
Was it priestly power?

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.530
Or was it by some other means?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.650
It may prove to be our salvation.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.400
It won't.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.820
It will not be our salvation.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.350
What we engaged in was cannibalism.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.830
We fed on our fallen friends.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:06.960
At the time, our tribe found itself
in a similarly dire situation

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:10.090
owing to a shortage of food.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:14.220
However, one day,
the chief came to us with food--

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.350
bright red meat.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:21.650
All of us were vaguely aware
of where the meat came from.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.230
After all, whenever the chief
brought us the meat,

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.190
it was invariably after
he had expelled a family

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.110
who had violated our strict laws.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:33.120
We simply closed our eyes, and ate the meat.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.580
In order to survive.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:40.330
Still, it wasn't as though
that could go on indefinitely.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.960
Before long, the pent-up frustration
came to an explosive head,

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.380
and manifested itself
in the form of an insurrection.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.670
I, as the one who was the
second-most-powerful next to the chief,

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:53.200
became the banner they rallied to,
and we rose in revolt against the chief.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.260
The fighting divided the village in two,

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:59.590
but with our greater numbers,
we were the ones who secured victory.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:04.060
The chief refused
to back down to the very end,

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:07.020
and after receiving countless wounds,
he was on the verge of death.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.400
Then, at the moment
when the fatal blow was struck,

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.400
he smiled at me.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.180
It was a truly sweet smile.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:22.000
Through the death of the chief,
the tribe was brought back together.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.000
Moreover, since our numbers
had decreased,

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.420
the great gift of recovery
from our food situation came with it.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.920
We were in the wrong, weren't we?

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.590
The chief, who acted out of
a clear view of reality,

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.990
was actually the one in the right, wasn't he?

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.510
I can't shake those thoughts.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.230
We are neither omniscient nor omnipotent.

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.440
If I were in your position,
I might have done the same thing.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.150
But I don't want to offer you solace.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:57.320
Are there ever any
correct answers in this world?

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.290
The only thing we can do is keep walking,

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:03.710
even as we afflict the soles
of our feet with woe and remorse.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.790
You, too, must keep walking.
That's what I think.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.340
I'm sorry you had to
see me look so disgraceful.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:16.870
What disgrace?

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:21.180
What's more, do I look like a male
who's foolish enough to believe

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.890
that anyone who
keeps moving along their road,

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:26.230
even as they are tormented
and scarred by it, is disgraceful?

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.730
You are beautiful.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.530
Yikes...

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:37.700
Let me ask you once again.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.700
Which policy will the Red Eye adopt?

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:44.200
After our discussion yesterday,
we have decided on evacuation.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:48.130
Then let me ask you,
Acting Chief Crusch Lulu,

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.710
do you still feel the same?

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:58.970
It is for you to decide. When the
previous chief smiled at you at the end,

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.640
it was because he was
giving this future over to you.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.930
If true, now is the time
for you to fulfill that calling.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.980
In that case, let me ask you,

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.480
how many do you plan on
letting escape as refugees?

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:18.160
Ten from the warrior class,
12 hunters, 3 priests,

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:21.490
70 males, 100 females,
and a number of children.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.050
And other than them?

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.250
If the situation calls for it, they will die.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:29.820
I see.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:35.260
There's one thing I'd like to make clear--
we are not fighting to die.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.240
We're fighting to win!

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:43.760
In that case, we of the Red Eye
will fight with you.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:47.320
To make sure our chief's smile
was not meaningless.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:52.530
As well as to ensure that as many of
the Red Eye tribe as possible will survive.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:55.600
You have my gratitude.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:09.250
Good morning.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.250
Yeah, good morning.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:14.250
It looks like you brought the tribe
around without any issue.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.470
I'm grateful that you took part
in the discussions until so late last night.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:21.510
Those who will fight should be able
to leave within the day.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.990
Those who are evacuating, as well.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:27.560
Zaryusu, what will you do now?

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:31.020
I plan to head over
to the Dragon Tusk tribe.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.940
Although, I do have a question...

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.450
What's with that getup?

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.400
It doesn't look good on me?

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:41.280
Would you like me to say
it looks good on you?

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:45.490
Don't be silly. The light of the sun
is hard on me when I'm out and about.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.040
You're planning to come with me?

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:51.920
The Dragon Tusk have the greatest
force of arms of all the tribes, right?

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:55.920
Yeah. But since we have no dealings
with them, we're not well informed.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:58.920
Then it's best that I go with you.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:00.760
It will be dangerous.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.930
Is there anywhere right now
that <i>isn't</i> dangerous?

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.930
I'm not thinking rationally, am I?

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.480
All right. I'll avail myself
of your help, Crusch.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:15.010
Very well, Zaryusu. You can count on me.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.450
These are the teleportation scrolls,

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.200
and the "Message" scrolls.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.740
Lord Ains said they were made
from parchment that we obtained

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.040
through the efforts of Lord Demiurge.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:36.040
He says that he wants us to report
if we have any problems using them.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.210
I see. Understood.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.340
So once again, Demiurge has
distinguished himself over me.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:43.530
Also...

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:50.680
...we have been instructed to monitor
the outcome of the battle from here.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.310
Understood.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:55.520
I want you to see this through,

00:20:55.520 --> 00:21:00.110
and deliver an absolute victory
for the Supreme One!

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:12.540
"Dragon Tusk Tribe Village"

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:22.360
I am Zaryusu Shasha. I am here
on behalf of the Green Claw tribe.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.590
I wish to speak to your chief.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:28.120
I am acting chief of
the Red Eye tribe, Crusch Lulu.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.850
I, too, am here to meet with your chief.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:36.430
I'm glad you came, possessor of Frost Pain.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:42.480
And what might you be,
some kind of plant monster?

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:43.610
No, I'm not!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:47.280
Oh, please, don't take my joke so seriously.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:52.120
I am the Dragon Tusk chief, Zenberu Gugu.
You can call me Zenberu.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:56.210
You are free to call me Zaryusu,
as well. Now...

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:59.130
I can already guess
what you're going to say.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.800
However, we only trust
those who are strong.

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:06.090
Take up your sword.
